  "pages": [
    {
      "doc_id": "d01",
      "page_index": 0,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000001",
      "text": "MOUNTAIN VIEW REGIONAL EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT\nPatient: TESTPATIENT, ALEX   DOB: 01/01/1980   MRN: 000111\nArrival: 03/14/2024 18:42  Mode: private vehicle\nChief complaint: neck pain after motor vehicle collision\nHPI: 44 y/o restrained driver, rear-ended at a stoplight approx 1 hr prior. Reports posterior neck pain 6/10, denies LOC, denies numbness or tingling.\nExam: Paraspinal tenderness C4-C6. No midline tenderness. Strength 5/5 bilateral upper extremities.\nAssessment: Cervical strain.\nDisposition: Discharged home with ibuprofen. Follow up with PCP in 1 week.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "ed_note"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d01",
      "page_index": 1,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000002",
      "text": "RADIOLOGY REPORT\nExam: XR CERVICAL SPINE 3 VIEWS\nClinical indication: neck pain after MVC\nComparison: None.\nFindings: Normal alignment. Vertebral body heights are maintained. Mild disc space narrowing at C5-C6 with small anterior osteophytes. No acute fracture. Prevertebral soft tissues within normal limits.\nImpression: No acute fracture. Mild degenerative changes at C5-C6.\nElectronically signed by: R. Example, MD",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "imaging_report"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d01",
      "page_index": 2,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000003",
      "text": "ED TRIAGE NOTE\nTriage time 21:05  ESI level 4\nVitals: BP 132/84 HR 88 RR 16 SpO2 99% T 98.4F\nReason for visit: low back pain, slipped on wet floor at work\nPain score 7/10. Ambulatory with steady gait. No bowel or bladder changes reported.\nTriage RN: J. Example, RN",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "ed_note"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d02",
      "page_index": 0,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000004",
      "text": "FAMILY MEDICINE ASSOCIATES - PROGRESS NOTE\nDate of service: 03/21/2024\nSubjective: Follow up for neck pain since MVC on 03/14/2024. Pain improved from 6/10 to 4/10. Some stiffness in the mornings. Sleeping better.\nObjective: Decreased cervical rotation to the right. No neurological deficits.\nAssessment/Plan: 1. Cervical strain, improving. Refer to physical therapy 2x/week for 6 weeks. Continue NSAIDs as needed. Return in 4 weeks.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "office_visit"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d03",
      "page_index": 0,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000005",
      "text": "PHYSICAL THERAPY DAILY NOTE  Visit 4 of 12\nDx: Cervical strain (S16.1XXA)\nPatient reports 3/10 neck pain today, able to drive 30 minutes without increase in symptoms.\nTreatment: Manual therapy 15 min, therapeutic exercise 20 min (chin tucks, scapular retraction, thoracic extension), moist heat 10 min.\nAssessment: Improving cervical ROM, rotation now 60 deg bilaterally.\nPlan: Continue per plan of care. Progress to resisted rows next visit.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "therapy_note"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d03",
      "page_index": 1,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000006",
      "text": "PATIENT EDUCATION: HOME EXERCISES FOR NECK PAIN\n1. Chin tucks: sit tall, gently draw your chin straight back. Hold 5 seconds. Repeat 10 times.\n2. Shoulder rolls: roll shoulders backward in a slow circle 10 times.\nStop any exercise that causes sharp pain and contact your provider.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "other"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d04",
      "page_index": 0,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000007",
      "text": "CHIROPRACTIC TREATMENT RECORD\nDate: 04/02/2024\nSubjective: Lower back tight, 5/10, worse after sitting.\nSegments adjusted: L4, L5, SI joint right.\nModalities: electrical stimulation 12 minutes, intersegmental traction.\nResponse to treatment: patient tolerated well, reports decreased tightness post adjustment.\nNext visit: 04/05/2024",
      "text_source": "ocr",
      "ocr_confidence": 0.62,
      "page_type": "therapy_note"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d05",
      "page_index": 0,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000008",
      "text": "ORTHOPEDIC CONSULTATION\nReferring provider: Dr. Sample\nHistory: Right shoulder pain for 3 months. Patient reports a prior shoulder injury playing softball in 2019, resolved without treatment.\nExam: Positive Neer and Hawkins on the right. Full passive range of motion.\nImpression: Right shoulder impingement, rule out rotator cuff tear.\nPlan: MRI right shoulder without contrast. Subacromial injection offered, patient will consider.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "office_visit"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d05",
      "page_index": 1,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000009",
      "text": "MRI RIGHT SHOULDER WITHOUT CONTRAST\nTechnique: Multiplanar multisequence MR imaging of the right shoulder.\nFindings: Partial thickness articular surface tear of the supraspinatus tendon measuring 6 mm. Mild subacromial-subdeltoid bursitis. Type II acromion. Labrum intact.\nIMPRESSION:\n1. Partial thickness supraspinatus tear.\n2. Mild bursitis.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "imaging_report"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d05",
      "page_index": 2,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000010",
      "text": "PROCEDURE NOTE\nProcedure: Right subacromial corticosteroid injection under ultrasound guidance\nIndication: Right shoulder impingement\nConsent: Risks including infection, bleeding and tendon weakening discussed; written consent obtained.\nTechnique: Skin prepped with chlorhexidine. 25-gauge needle advanced into the subacromial space under direct visualization. Injected 40 mg triamcinolone with 4 mL 1% lidocaine.\nComplications: None. Patient tolerated the procedure well.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "procedure_report"
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "d05",
      "page_index": 3,
      "bates_label": "SYN 000011",
      "text": "OPERATIVE REPORT\nPreoperative diagnosis: Right shoulder rotator cuff tear\nPostoperative diagnosis: Same\nProcedure: Arthroscopic rotator cuff repair, subacromial decompression\nAnesthesia: General with interscalene block\nEstimated blood loss: minimal\nFindings: Full thickness tear of the supraspinatus, 1.5 cm. Repaired with two suture anchors.\nThe patient was taken to recovery in stable condition.",
      "text_source": "native",
      "ocr_confidence": null,
      "page_type": "procedure_report"
    },
